    "body": "`pytest.approx` returns `False` for two finite `Decimal` values even though their exact difference is below the requested `Decimal` tolerance.\n\n## Reproducer\n\n```python\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\nimport pytest\n\nexpected = Decimal(\"1e400\")\nactual = Decimal(\"1.0000001e400\")\nrel = Decimal(\"0.000001\")\ndifference = abs(actual - expected)\ntolerance = rel * abs(expected)\n\nprint(\"difference:\", difference)\nprint(\"tolerance:\", tolerance)\nprint(\"both finite:\", expected.is_finite() and actual.is_finite())\nprint(\"in tolerance:\", difference < tolerance)\nprint(\"relative comparison:\", actual == pytest.approx(expected, rel=rel))\nprint(\"absolute comparison:\", actual == pytest.approx(expected, abs=tolerance))\n```\n\nOutput on pytest 9.1.1:\n\n```text\ndifference: 1E+393\ntolerance: 1E+394\nboth finite: True\nin tolerance: True\nrelative comparison: False\nabsolute comparison: False\n```\n\nBoth comparisons should be `True`. The same result occurs on current `main` at `3fd8675d6d798507c06cf9c60753be6d9d7b0e17`.\n\nThis appears to happen because [the infinity guard](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/blob/3fd8675d6d798507c06cf9c60753be6d9d7b0e17/src/_pytest/approx.py#L538) calls `math.isinf(abs(self.expected))`, which treats finite `Decimal(\"1e400\")` as binary-float infinity before the exact Decimal tolerance is used.\n\nEnvironment: CPython 3.12.3, Ubuntu 24.04.4 LTS, Linux 6.8.0-100-generic x86-64. Reproduced on pytest 9.1.1 and the current `main` commit above.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Installed packages</summary>\n\n```text\nPackage          Version\n---------------- -------\nattrs            26.1.0\nhypothesis       6.168.0\niniconfig        2.3.0\nnumpy            2.5.3\npackaging        26.3\npluggy           1.6.0\npygments         2.21.0\npytest           9.1.1\nsortedcontainers 2.4.0\n```\n\n</details>\n\nThe closest reports I found, [#8495](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/8495) and [#3247](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/3247), concern different Decimal failures.\n\nAI tools assisted with discovery and independent verification. I reviewed and reproduced this issue.\n",
